# Environment Secrets

Never commit API keys, database passwords, tokens, or other secrets in source. Load them from the environment via `dotenv`; keep real values in `.env` (gitignored).

## Do / Don't

```typescript
// ❌ BAD — secrets in source or committed config
const apiKey = "sk-live-abc123";
const dbUrl = "postgres://admin:password@db/prod";

// ✅ GOOD — load from env (dotenv in local/dev)
import "dotenv/config";

const apiKey = process.env.API_KEY;
const dbUrl = process.env.DATABASE_URL;
```

## Checklist

- Add `.env` to `.gitignore` (and do not force-add it).
- Use `dotenv` (or `import "dotenv/config"`) so local/dev reads `.env`.
- Commit only `.env.example` with placeholder names — never real credentials.
- In production, prefer the host’s secret manager / injected env vars over shipping a `.env` file.
- Never hardcode secrets in TypeScript, JSON, shell scripts, or docs checked into the repo.
